# Component Architecture Standards

## Component Organization
- **Pages**: High-level views (project-view, form-view)
- **Sections**: Grouped functionality (component-palette, form-canvas) 
- **Units**: Reusable components (button, radio, input)

## Component Structure Standards
- `component.html`: Semantic and component-based markup
- `component.scss`: Component-specific styling only
- `component.ts`: Component logic and state management (max 300 lines)
- `component.service.ts`: External logic and API calls

## Reusable Component Pattern
```typescript
// Instead of inline buttons
<button type="button" class="cancel-btn" (click)="cancel()">Cancel</button>
<button type="button" class="btn publish-btn create-btn" (click)="submitForm()">Submit</button>

// Use component-based approach
<form-button [text]="'Cancel'" [type]="'cancel'" (onClick)="cancel()"></form-button>
<form-button [text]="'Submit'" [type]="'primary'" (onClick)="submitForm()"></form-button>
```

## Abstraction Layers
- Move complex logic to services
- Keep components focused on presentation
- Use shared services for common functionality
- Implement proper separation of concerns

## Asset Management
- Use SVG icons instead of PNG
- Clear descriptive names: `arrow-up.svg`, `arrow-down.svg` (not `up-arrow.svg`)
- Group related assets logically
- Remove redundant files: avoid both `edit.png` and `edit.svg`

## Translation Support
- Add translation keys for all user-facing text
- Use enums for message constants
- Support dynamic content translation
